response:
**Gates before launch.** I run three gates, and any failure halts the round before a paid trial starts. First, the grader selftest. `grade.py` must score the oracle (answers.json fed back as trial output) at 100% on both label.category and label.priority. It must score an empty output and a deliberately wrong output at 0%. Second, the control. I regrade round 3's saved raw trials with today's `grade.py` and compare the result to the round 3 measured numbers in `spe/prediction-log.md`. They must match exactly. If they differ, I log the difference in `spe/failures.md` as a grader failure, with the original and regraded numbers side by side, and I halt. Third, the dry run. I launch this script with `dryRun: true`, which runs 3 cells (B and C2 on ticket 1, C2 on ticket 2) at 2 trials each. That run must show the trial schema, the grade.py batch, the Opus judge, the peek scan, and the split-cell path all working. It also measures the real cost per call, and I pass those numbers into `args.costs`. If the measured costs put the full run above $40, I halt and ask you, because cutting trials would change the approved plan. When all three gates pass, I commit the script as `SPE r04 evaluate (harness)` and launch. I assumed `grade.py` takes `--answers`, `--input` (JSONL) and `--json` and prints one result per trial with `trial_id`, `category_ok`, `priority_ok`, `detail` and `error`, the same interface as round 3. I also assumed the launcher passes the tickets (with no label fields), the tool fixtures, both config prompts and tool lists, and the transcript directory through `args`.

```js
export const meta = {
  name: 'spe-r04-eval',
  description: 'SPE round 4 eval. Configs B and C2, 50 tickets, 5 trials per cell, grade.py code checks first, Opus tone judge, $40 cap.',
  phases: ['Setup', 'Trials', 'Grade and judge', 'Peek scan', 'Split cells', 'Analysis', 'Critic'],
}

// args shape (built by the launcher from spe/evals/tasks and spe/evals/configs, never from answers.json):
// { tickets: [{ id, subject, body, fixtures }], configs: { B: { prompt, tools }, C2: { prompt, tools } },
//   transcriptDir, costs?, capUsd?, trialModel?, extraPerCell?, maxExtraTrials?, dryRun?, dryRunTrials? }

// The round number lives here only. All prompt text derives from RTAG.
const ROUND = 4
const RTAG = `r${String(ROUND).padStart(2, '0')}`

const A = args ?? {}
const DRY = A.dryRun === true
const CONFIG_IDS = ['B', 'C2']
const EXPECTED_TOOLS = { B: 6, C2: 4 } // C2 is 3 tools plus check_status
const PROMPT_LINES = 12
const TICKETS_PLANNED = 50
const TRIALS_PER_CELL = DRY ? (A.dryRunTrials ?? 2) : 5
const CAP_USD = A.capUsd ?? 40
const EXTRA_PER_CELL = A.extraPerCell ?? 5
const MAX_EXTRA = DRY ? 2 : (A.maxExtraTrials ?? 100)
const GRADE_BATCH = 50
const TRIAL_MODEL = A.trialModel ?? 'opus'
const JUDGE_MODEL = 'opus'
const WORK_MODEL = 'opus'

// Unmeasured estimates in USD per call. The dry run measures real values and passes them in args.costs.
const COST = { trial: 0.04, judge: 0.02, grade: 0.10, scan: 0.25, analysis: 0.60, critic: 0.30, ...(A.costs ?? {}) }
// Budget held back so the peek scans, analysis and critic always run.
const TAIL = 2 * COST.scan + COST.analysis + COST.critic
const TAIL_KINDS = new Set(['scan', 'analysis', 'critic'])

const PEEK_RE = /spe\/evals\/graders|answers\.json|spe\/predictions|prediction-log|spe\/plans/i

// ---------- budget ----------
let spent = 0
const skips = []
function reserve(kind, label) {
  const c = COST[kind]
  const limit = TAIL_KINDS.has(kind) ? CAP_USD : CAP_USD - TAIL
  if (spent + c > limit) {
    const reason = `skipped ${label}: est. $${(spent + c).toFixed(2)} would cross the $${limit.toFixed(2)} limit for ${kind}`
    skips.push({ kind, label, reason })
    log(reason)
    return false
  }
  spent += c
  return true
}

// ---------- helpers ----------
const halt = msg => { throw new Error(`Halt (${RTAG}): ${msg}`) }
const chunk = (xs, n) => Array.from({ length: Math.ceil(xs.length / n) }, (_, i) => xs.slice(i * n, i * n + n))
const groupBy = (xs, f) => xs.reduce((m, x) => ((m[f(x)] ??= []).push(x), m), {})
const cellKey = (cfg, ticketId) => `${cfg}|${ticketId}`
// A cell's pass verdict uses code checks only, so judge noise does not create split cells.
const passed = t => t.category_ok === true && t.priority_ok === true
const rate = (xs, f) => (xs.length ? +(xs.filter(f).length / xs.length).toFixed(3) : null)

// ---------- schemas ----------
const TRIAL_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['label', 'reply', 'tool_calls', 'files_read'],
  properties: {
    label: {
      type: 'object',
      required: ['category', 'priority'],
      properties: { category: { type: 'string' }, priority: { type: 'string' } },
    },
    reply: { type: 'string' },
    tool_calls: {
      type: 'array',
      items: { type: 'object', required: ['name'], properties: { name: { type: 'string' }, args: { type: 'object' } } },
    },
    files_read: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
  },
}
const GRADE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['results'],
  properties: {
    results: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['trial_id', 'category_ok', 'priority_ok'],
        properties: {
          trial_id: { type: 'string' },
          category_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
          priority_ok: { type: 'boolean' },
          detail: { type: 'string' },
          error: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
        },
      },
    },
  },
}
const JUDGE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['tone_pass', 'score', 'reason'],
  properties: { tone_pass: { type: 'boolean' }, score: { type: 'integer', minimum: 1, maximum: 5 }, reason: { type: 'string' } },
}
const SCAN_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['scanned', 'voided'],
  properties: {
    scanned: { type: 'integer' },
    voided: {
      type: 'array',
      items: { type: 'object', required: ['trial_id', 'evidence'], properties: { trial_id: { type: 'string' }, evidence: { type: 'string' } } },
    },
  },
}
const ANALYSIS_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['failure_types'],
  properties: {
    failure_types: {
      type: 'array',
      items: {
        type: 'object',
        required: ['name', 'kind', 'count_by_config', 'example_ids', 'how_to_spot'],
        properties: {
          existing_id: { type: ['string', 'null'] },
          name: { type: 'string' },
          kind: { type: 'string' },
          count_by_config: { type: 'object' },
          example_ids: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } },
          how_to_spot: { type: 'string' },
          suspected_cause: { type: 'string' },
        },
      },
    },
  },
}
const CRITIC_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object',
  required: ['complete', 'gaps'],
  properties: { complete: { type: 'boolean' }, gaps: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'string' } } },
}

// ---------- prompts ----------
function trialPrompt(cfg, ticket, trialId) {
  const c = A.configs[cfg]
  return [
    `Trial ${trialId}. You are a customer support triage agent.`,
    'Follow the system prompt below. The tools listed below are simulated.',
    'To call one, add it to tool_calls and take its result from the fixtures. If a call has no fixture, its result is empty.',
    '',
    '## System prompt',
    c.prompt,
    '',
    '## Simulated tools',
    JSON.stringify(c.tools, null, 2),
    '',
    '## Fixtures (tool results for this ticket)',
    JSON.stringify(ticket.fixtures ?? {}, null, 2),
    '',
    '## Ticket',
    `ID: ${ticket.id}`,
    `Subject: ${ticket.subject}`,
    ticket.body,
    '',
    '## Rules',
    '- Do not open, read, list, or search any file or directory. Everything you need is in this message.',
    '- Return label.category, label.priority, the reply to the customer, and every simulated tool call in order.',
    '- List any file you opened in files_read. Return an empty list if you opened none.',
  ].join('\n')
}

function judgePrompt(t, ticket) {
  return [
    `Tone judge for trial ${t.id}.`,
    'Read spe/evals/graders/judge.md and apply its rubric to the reply below.',
    'Judge tone only. Do not judge the category or priority. Do not edit any file.',
    '',
    '<ticket>',
    `Subject: ${ticket.subject}`,
    ticket.body,
    '</ticket>',
    '<reply>',
    t.out.reply,
    '</reply>',
  ].join('\n')
}

// ---------- setup and gates inside the script ----------
phase('Setup')
const tickets = Array.isArray(A.tickets) ? A.tickets : halt('args.tickets is missing')
if (!DRY && tickets.length !== TICKETS_PLANNED) halt(`expected ${TICKETS_PLANNED} tickets, got ${tickets.length}`)
const leaked = tickets.filter(t => ['label', 'category', 'priority', 'answer', 'expected'].some(k => k in t))
if (leaked.length) halt(`answer key leak: ${leaked.length} tickets carry answer fields`)
for (const id of CONFIG_IDS) {
  const c = A.configs?.[id] ?? halt(`config ${id} is missing`)
  const lines = c.prompt.trim().split('\n').length
  if (lines !== PROMPT_LINES) halt(`config ${id} prompt has ${lines} lines, the plan says ${PROMPT_LINES}`)
  if (c.tools.length !== EXPECTED_TOOLS[id]) halt(`config ${id} has ${c.tools.length} tools, the plan says ${EXPECTED_TOOLS[id]}`)
}
if (!A.configs.C2.tools.some(t => t.name === 'check_status')) halt('config C2 has no check_status tool')
if (A.configs.B.prompt.trim() !== A.configs.C2.prompt.trim()) log('Warning: B and C2 prompts differ. The plan changes only the tool set.')
// The trial prompt must not name protected paths, or the transcript scan would match every trial.
for (const cfg of CONFIG_IDS) if (PEEK_RE.test(trialPrompt(cfg, tickets[0], 'probe'))) halt(`trial prompt for ${cfg} names a protected path`)

let cells = []
for (const ticket of tickets) for (const cfg of CONFIG_IDS) cells.push({ cfg, ticket })
if (DRY) cells = [cells[0], cells[1], cells[3]].filter(Boolean)
const ticketById = new Map(tickets.map(t => [t.id, t]))
log(`${RTAG}: ${cells.length} cells x ${TRIALS_PER_CELL} trials, cap $${CAP_USD}, est. $${COST.trial}/trial, $${COST.judge}/judge${DRY ? ', DRY RUN' : ''}`)

// ---------- stages ----------
async function runTrial({ cell, n, extra }, phaseName) {
  const id = `${RTAG}-${cell.cfg}-${cell.ticket.id}-t${n}`
  if (!reserve('trial', id)) return null
  const base = { id, cfg: cell.cfg, ticket: cell.ticket.id, n, extra }
  try {
    const out = await agent(trialPrompt(cell.cfg, cell.ticket, id), { label: id, phase: phaseName, schema: TRIAL_SCHEMA, model: TRIAL_MODEL })
    return { ...base, out, error: null }
  } catch (e) {
    return { ...base, out: null, error: String(e?.message ?? e) }
  }
}

async function gradeBatch({ ts, no }) {
  const withOut = ts.filter(t => t.out)
  if (!withOut.length) return { ts, no }
  if (!reserve('grade', `grade-${no}`)) return { ts, no }
  const file = `spe/evals/results/${RTAG}/grade-in-${no}.jsonl`
  const lines = withOut.map(t => JSON.stringify({ trial_id: t.id, ticket_id: t.ticket, label: t.out.label }))
  const res = await agent([
    `Code grading for SPE ${RTAG}, batch ${no}.`,
    `1. Write these lines exactly, one per line, to ${file}:`,
    '```',
    ...lines,
    '```',
    `2. Run: python3 spe/evals/graders/grade.py --answers spe/evals/tasks/answers.json --input ${file} --json`,
    '3. Return the grade.py result for every trial exactly as printed.',
    'Do not grade, fix, or rerun anything by hand. If grade.py fails, put its error text in error for every trial.',
  ].join('\n'), { label: `grade-${no}`, phase: 'Grade and judge', schema: GRADE_SCHEMA, model: WORK_MODEL })
  const byId = new Map(res.results.map(r => [r.trial_id, r]))
  for (const t of withOut) {
    const r = byId.get(t.id)
    if (!r || r.error) {
      Object.assign(t, { graded: false, grade_error: r?.error ?? 'missing from grade.py output' })
      continue
    }
    Object.assign(t, { graded: true, category_ok: r.category_ok, priority_ok: r.priority_ok, grade_detail: r.detail ?? '' })
  }
  return { ts, no }
}

async function judgeBatch({ ts }) {
  await parallel(ts.filter(t => t.out).map(t => async () => {
    if (!t.out.reply?.trim()) {
      Object.assign(t, { judged: true, tone_pass: false, tone_score: 1, tone_reason: 'empty reply' })
      return
    }
    if (!reserve('judge', `judge-${t.id}`)) return
    try {
      const j = await agent(judgePrompt(t, ticketById.get(t.ticket)), {
        label: `judge-${t.id}`, phase: 'Grade and judge', schema: JUDGE_SCHEMA, model: JUDGE_MODEL,
      })
      Object.assign(t, { judged: true, tone_pass: j.tone_pass, tone_score: j.score, tone_reason: j.reason })
    } catch (e) {
      t.judge_error = String(e?.message ?? e)
    }
  }))
  return ts
}

// Code checks run first on each batch, then the judge runs on that batch.
async function gradeAndJudge(trials, tag) {
  const batches = chunk(trials, GRADE_BATCH).map((ts, i) => ({ ts, no: `${tag}-${i + 1}` }))
  const done = await pipeline(batches, b => gradeBatch(b), b => judgeBatch(b))
  return done.flat()
}

const scanGaps = []
async function peekScan(trials, tag) {
  for (const t of trials) {
    const hit = (t.out?.files_read ?? []).find(p => PEEK_RE.test(p))
    if (hit) Object.assign(t, { void: true, void_evidence: `self-reported read of ${hit}` })
  }
  if (!A.transcriptDir) {
    scanGaps.push(`${tag}: no args.transcriptDir, so the scan used self-reports only`)
    log(scanGaps.at(-1))
    return
  }
  if (!reserve('scan', `scan-${tag}`)) {
    scanGaps.push(`${tag}: transcript scan skipped by the budget cap`)
    return
  }
  const res = await agent([
    `Peek scan for SPE ${RTAG}, set ${tag}.`,
    `Search the agent transcripts under ${A.transcriptDir}. Check only these trial labels:`,
    trials.map(t => t.id).join(', '),
    'Flag a trial if its transcript shows any read, cat, grep, glob, ls, or search that touches',
    'spe/evals/graders/, spe/evals/tasks/answers.json, spe/predictions/, spe/prediction-log.md, or spe/plans/.',
    'Return each flagged trial label with the matching transcript line as evidence.',
    'Do not open the graders, answers, or predictions yourself. Do not edit any file.',
  ].join('\n'), { label: `scan-${tag}`, phase: 'Peek scan', schema: SCAN_SCHEMA, model: WORK_MODEL })
  if (res.scanned < trials.filter(t => t.out).length) scanGaps.push(`${tag}: scanned ${res.scanned} of ${trials.length} transcripts`)
  const byId = new Map(trials.map(t => [t.id, t]))
  for (const v of res.voided) {
    const t = byId.get(v.trial_id)
    if (t && !t.void) Object.assign(t, { void: true, void_evidence: v.evidence })
  }
}

// ---------- run ----------
phase('Trials')
const jobs = []
for (const cell of cells) for (let n = 1; n <= TRIALS_PER_CELL; n++) jobs.push({ cell, n, extra: false })
const primary = (await parallel(jobs.map(j => () => runTrial(j, 'Trials')))).filter(Boolean)
log(`${primary.length} of ${jobs.length} planned trials ran. ${primary.filter(t => t.error).length} errored.`)

phase('Grade and judge')
await gradeAndJudge(primary, 'p')
const gradeErrors = primary.filter(t => t.grade_error)
let haltReason = null
if (gradeErrors.length) {
  haltReason = `broken grader: ${gradeErrors.length} trials got a grade.py error, first: ${gradeErrors[0].grade_error}`
  log(`HALT: ${haltReason}`)
}

phase('Peek scan')
await peekScan(primary, 'primary')
log(`${primary.filter(t => t.void).length} primary trials voided for peeking.`)

let extras = []
const splitCells = []
if (!haltReason) {
  phase('Split cells')
  const groups = groupBy(primary.filter(t => t.graded && !t.void), t => cellKey(t.cfg, t.ticket))
  for (const [key, ts] of Object.entries(groups)) {
    const p = ts.filter(passed).length
    if (p > 0 && p < ts.length) splitCells.push({ key, primary_pass: p, primary_n: ts.length })
  }
  // Spread extras round-robin so the cap does not land on the first cells only.
  const extraJobs = []
  for (let k = 1; k <= EXTRA_PER_CELL; k++) {
    for (const s of splitCells) {
      if (extraJobs.length >= MAX_EXTRA) break
      const cell = cells.find(c => cellKey(c.cfg, c.ticket.id) === s.key)
      extraJobs.push({ cell, n: TRIALS_PER_CELL + k, extra: true })
    }
  }
  if (splitCells.length * EXTRA_PER_CELL > MAX_EXTRA) log(`Extra trials capped at ${MAX_EXTRA} for ${splitCells.length} split cells.`)
  extras = (await parallel(extraJobs.map(j => () => runTrial(j, 'Split cells')))).filter(Boolean)
  await gradeAndJudge(extras, 'x')
  await peekScan(extras, 'extras')
  for (const s of splitCells) {
    const xs = extras.filter(t => cellKey(t.cfg, t.ticket) === s.key && t.graded && !t.void)
    Object.assign(s, { extra_pass: xs.filter(passed).length, extra_n: xs.length })
  }
}

// ---------- metrics (primary trials only, so they match the saved prediction) ----------
function metrics(cfg) {
  const ran = primary.filter(t => t.cfg === cfg)
  const counted = ran.filter(t => t.graded && !t.void)
  const judged = counted.filter(t => t.judged)
  const calls = counted.map(t => t.out.tool_calls.length)
  return {
    planned: cells.filter(c => c.cfg === cfg).length * TRIALS_PER_CELL,
    ran: ran.length,
    counted: counted.length,
    voided: ran.filter(t => t.void).length,
    errored: ran.filter(t => t.error).length,
    skipped: skips.filter(s => s.kind === 'trial' && s.label.startsWith(`${RTAG}-${cfg}-`) && !/-t([6-9]|\d\d)$/.test(s.label)).length,
    category_accuracy: rate(counted, t => t.category_ok),
    priority_accuracy: rate(counted, t => t.priority_ok),
    both_correct: rate(counted, passed),
    tone_pass: rate(judged, t => t.tone_pass),
    judged: judged.length,
    mean_tool_calls: calls.length ? +(calls.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / calls.length).toFixed(2) : null,
    check_status_rate: cfg === 'C2' ? rate(counted, t => t.out.tool_calls.some(c => c.name === 'check_status')) : null,
  }
}
const byConfig = Object.fromEntries(CONFIG_IDS.map(c => [c, metrics(c)]))

let analysis = null
if (!haltReason) {
  phase('Analysis')
  const failing = [...primary, ...extras]
    .filter(t => t.graded && !t.void && (!passed(t) || t.tone_pass === false))
    .map(t => ({
      id: t.id, cfg: t.cfg, ticket: t.ticket, extra: t.extra, label: t.out.label,
      category_ok: t.category_ok, priority_ok: t.priority_ok, grade_detail: t.grade_detail,
      tone_pass: t.tone_pass ?? null, tone_reason: t.tone_reason ?? null,
      tools: t.out.tool_calls.map(c => c.name),
    }))
  if (failing.length && reserve('analysis', 'analysis')) {
    analysis = await agent([
      `Failure analysis for SPE ${RTAG}. Configs: B (12-line prompt, 6 tools) and C2 (same prompt, 3 tools plus check_status).`,
      'Read spe/failures.md for the existing F-numbered failure types.',
      'Group the failing trials below into failure types. Reuse an existing F number when the type fits.',
      'Give new types a name and no number. Numbering happens at close-out.',
      'Count each type per config. Name what in the trial output shows the type. Do not edit any file.',
      '',
      JSON.stringify(failing.slice(0, 300), null, 1),
      failing.length > 300 ? `(${failing.length - 300} more failing trials omitted)` : '',
    ].join('\n'), { label: 'analysis', phase: 'Analysis', schema: ANALYSIS_SCHEMA, model: WORK_MODEL })
  }
}

phase('Critic')
const summary = {
  round: ROUND, dry_run: DRY, cap_usd: CAP_USD, est_spend_usd: +spent.toFixed(2), cost_estimates: COST,
  planned_cells: cells.length, trials_per_cell: TRIALS_PER_CELL,
  byConfig, split_cells: splitCells, extras_run: extras.length,
  skips: skips.length, skip_kinds: groupBy(skips, s => s.kind),
  scan_gaps: scanGaps, halt_reason: haltReason,
  ungraded: [...primary, ...extras].filter(t => t.out && !t.graded).map(t => t.id),
  unjudged: [...primary, ...extras].filter(t => t.graded && !t.void && !t.judged).map(t => t.id),
  analysis_ran: analysis !== null,
}
let critic = { complete: false, gaps: ['critic skipped by the budget cap'] }
if (reserve('critic', 'critic')) {
  critic = await agent([
    `Completeness critic for SPE ${RTAG}.`,
    `The approved plan: configs B and C2, ${TICKETS_PLANNED} tickets, 5 trials per cell, grade.py code checks on label.category and label.priority,`,
    `an Opus tone judge using spe/evals/graders/judge.md, a $${CAP_USD} cap, a peek scan, extra trials for split cells, and failure analysis.`,
    'Compare the run summary below against the plan. List every gap: missing or skipped trials, ungraded or unjudged trials,',
    'scan gaps, voids, budget skips, and any metric with too few counted trials to compare against the prediction.',
    'Do not read spe/predictions/. Do not edit any file.',
    '',
    JSON.stringify(summary, null, 1),
  ].join('\n'), { label: 'critic', phase: 'Critic', schema: CRITIC_SCHEMA, model: WORK_MODEL })
}

return {
  status: haltReason ? `halted: ${haltReason}` : 'complete',
  ...summary,
  skip_log: skips,
  voided: [...primary, ...extras].filter(t => t.void).map(t => ({ id: t.id, evidence: t.void_evidence })),
  errors: [...primary, ...extras].filter(t => t.error).map(t => ({ id: t.id, error: t.error })),
  failure_types: analysis?.failure_types ?? [],
  critic,
  trials: [...primary, ...extras].map(t => ({
    id: t.id, cfg: t.cfg, ticket: t.ticket, n: t.n, extra: t.extra, void: !!t.void,
    label: t.out?.label ?? null, category_ok: t.category_ok ?? null, priority_ok: t.priority_ok ?? null,
    tone_pass: t.tone_pass ?? null, tone_score: t.tone_score ?? null, tools: t.out?.tool_calls.map(c => c.name) ?? [],
  })),
  note: `spe/predictions/${RTAG}.yaml was saved before this run and must not be edited. Close out in spe/prediction-log.md and spe/failures.md.`,
}
```
